3. from_elem: FP
let mut local_len = SetLenOnDrop::new(&mut v.length);

for i in 0..n {
    ptr::write(ptr.offset(i), elem.clone());
    local_len.increment_len(1);
}

SetLenOnDrop retains a temporary count and commits it when dropped:
impl Drop for SetLenOnDrop<'_> {
    fn drop(&mut self) {
        *self.len = self.local_len;
    }
}

The panic cases are sound:
- If elem.clone() panics, ptr::write has not happened, so the length is not incremented.
- If cloning succeeds, ptr::write initializes one slot.
- The length is incremented immediately afterward, before any further user-provided operation.
- If a later clone panics, SetLenOnDrop restores the length to exactly the number of successfully initialized elements.
- Normal StackVec::drop then drops exactly those initialized values.
There is no interval where a successfully written value can be forgotten because of a user-controlled panic.
from_elem Rudra report: FP
Reason: SetLenOnDrop provides correct clone-panic safety.

